        "# Key Information Extraction from Scanned Receipts\n",
        "## Deep Learning Final Project — ICDAR 2019 SROIE\n",
        "\n",
        "**Problem:** Convert scanned receipt images into a structured record with fields: `company`, `date`, `address`, `total`. Real receipts are noisy (low contrast, rotations, irregular layouts, mixed formats), so naive parsing is unreliable.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How I solve it:** I build an end-to-end pipeline and compare two approaches:\n",
        "1) a **classical baseline** using OCR (Tesseract) + simple regex rules, and\n",
        "2) a **deep learning model**, **Donut** (an OCR-free vision encoder/decoder) that predicts the target fields directly as JSON from pixels.\n",
        "\n",
        "**ML approach:** Supervised fine tuning of Donut on the public. **ICDAR 2019 SROIE** dataset (pulled from Hugging Face). Model selection uses validation loss; performance is reported with field-level metrics that include tolerant comparisons for both money and dates.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Evaluation & deliverables:** I report `total_within_1c`, `date_match`, `company_exact`, and `address_exact` on the validation split; export a CSV of predictions for a held-out test subset; and provide a model comparison table to substantiate conclusions."
      ],
